CaptionFast — Cursor Rules
B2B Windows Desktop Utility for Corporate Event Photographers
Architecture
Frontend: Flutter Windows Desktop (main.dart is single source of truth).

Backend: DigitalOcean FastAPI Proxy (No local servers, no Python locally).

ExifTool: Run via Process.run(), located using Platform.resolvedExecutable.

Security & State
NO client-side secrets. Use hardcoded proxy url.

NO Provider/Riverpod. Use setState.

NO third-party grid/selection packages. Use native GestureDetector + HardwareKeyboard.

V1.1 Core Workflow (Canonical)
State Variables (Strictly one-word lowercase)
anchorpath: String? — OCR source, set on click

selectedphotos: Set — batch write targets

processedfiles: Set — session green badge tracking

tagcontroller: TextEditingController — subject name field

viplist: Set — lowercase parsed VIP names

licensekey: String? — LemonSqueezy validated key

Phase 0: Safety Check
On initState: verify exiftool.exe exists via Platform.resolvedExecutable. If missing: block entire UI.

Phase 1: Session Init
On folder load: clear processedfiles, selectedphotos, anchorpath, tagcontroller.
VIP list parser: strip titles/punctuation/numbers, lowercase, store to viplist.

Phase 2: Selection Model
Single click → set anchorpath (gold border).
Ctrl-click → toggle in/out of selectedphotos (blue border).
Shift-click → range select into selectedphotos (blue border).
anchorpath is NEVER added to selectedphotos.

Phase 3: OCR
Send only anchorpath to proxy.
Flutter pre-populates tagcontroller with result. User verifies/edits. Never auto-submit.

Phase 4: Assign Batch
VIP check: tagcontroller.text.toLowerCase() in viplist.
If VIP match: append -XMP:Label=Red to exiftool args.
Write to all files in selectedphotos.
On exitCode == 0: add to processedfiles.
On completion: clear selectedphotos, anchorpath, tagcontroller (DO NOT clear processedfiles).

Phase 5: Fallback
If tagcontroller.text not empty AND selectedphotos not empty: Assign Batch enabled. Bypasses OCR, works offline.

Build & Testing Sequence
Run Tests: flutter test

Build Command: flutter build windows --release